# Supabase Security and RLS

## Non-negotiables

- Keep RLS enabled on `profiles`, `documents`, and `document_shares`
- Never disable RLS to fix a query failure
- Never put service-role keys or secrets in frontend code or commits
- Never log or commit `.env` / credentials
- Do not run destructive SQL or reset the DB without explicit user approval
- Inspect `supabase/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql` before changing policies

## Permission model

| Action | Who |
|---|---|
| Read | Owner or shared user |
| Create | Authenticated user as owner (`owner_id = auth.uid()`) |
| Update | Owner or share with `permission = 'edit'` |
| Delete | Owner only |
| Manage shares | Owner only |

- Users must not escalate permissions or reassign ownership via client updates
- Private docs must stay inaccessible to unrelated users

## Cross-table policies

- Direct `documents` ↔ `document_shares` subqueries in RLS caused infinite recursion
- Use existing `SECURITY DEFINER` helpers: `is_document_owner`, `has_document_share`
- Review `USING` and `WITH CHECK` for SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE

## Verification

- Frontend UI checks are not authorization
- Do not claim RLS is verified without evidence (tests, SQL checks, or two-user manual tests)
- Prefer the `supabase-rls-security` skill for policy work
